WEBVTT

00:00:02.130 --> 00:00:04.700
Hi! Patty here.

00:00:04.930 --> 00:00:06.030
Tia here.

00:00:06.030 --> 00:00:07.490
Together, we are...

00:00:07.490 --> 00:00:09.130
Patty and Tia!

00:00:09.130 --> 00:00:11.320
We're the best ARKS information brokers.

00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:15.390
You have to give all the 
information you have to us.

00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:19.270
You'd better come clean quickly, 
before you make your mom cry.

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:22.100
That's not true, dummy.

00:00:22.730 --> 00:00:25.750
We just have some questions 
for you, so don't worry.

00:00:26.050 --> 00:00:29.750
Lately I feel like the number 
of ARKS has been on the rise.

00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:31.090
What do you think?

00:00:31.090 --> 00:00:35.400
It's good that there are more 
ARKS to exterminate the Darkers,

00:00:35.690 --> 00:00:39.640
but I've been curious lately,
since there are so many ARKS I don't know.

00:00:40.530 --> 00:00:43.280
It's suspicious that you 
haven't said anything yet.

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:46.490
Are you one of those mysterious ARKS?

00:00:46.490 --> 00:00:49.350
I think he's just too flabbergasted to talk.

00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:52.770
Or do you want us to give you information 
before you tell us anything?

00:00:52.770 --> 00:00:53.870
We can't do that!

00:00:53.870 --> 00:00:57.980
We're information brokers,
but we've got an exclusive contract.

00:00:57.980 --> 00:00:59.760
We're sworn to secrecy, secrecy!

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:03.630
I wish you'd stick to that 
and keep your mouth shut.

00:01:05.340 --> 00:01:08.210
I feel like talking again!

00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:10.360
Tia, we need to make a tactical retreat.

00:01:10.360 --> 00:01:11.300
Retreat!

00:01:11.890 --> 00:01:14.140
What kind of selfish reason is that?

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:15.650
Hey, wait!

00:01:17.050 --> 00:01:18.590
What was that all about?

00:01:18.870 --> 00:01:22.820
They called out to me out of the blue
and then ran away out of the blue.

00:01:23.470 --> 00:01:26.080
You're interested in those soulless persons?

00:01:26.330 --> 00:01:29.310
Soulless? What does that mean?

00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:33.430
It means they're Non-Player 
Characters, or NPCs.

00:01:33.430 --> 00:01:35.070
Wait, you dummy!

00:01:35.070 --> 00:01:37.950
Tia's mad!

00:03:07.830 --> 00:03:10.580
<b>Quest 05      Aika</b>

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:16.080
"It feels exactly like speaking 
with a high school girl."

00:03:16.660 --> 00:03:21.010
These are your thoughts 
on the humanity of NPCs?

00:03:21.010 --> 00:03:25.140
They seem more like living, 
breathing humans than programs.

00:03:25.850 --> 00:03:30.290
That's because they're programmed 
with the newest AI technology.

00:03:30.290 --> 00:03:33.510
I'm rejecting this delusional report that 
sounds like you're falling in love with a 2D girl.

00:03:33.940 --> 00:03:34.900
Rewrite this.

00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:36.590
What?

00:03:39.130 --> 00:03:40.130
What is it?

00:03:40.130 --> 00:03:41.650
You're very interesting.

00:03:41.650 --> 00:03:42.660
Huh?

00:03:44.410 --> 00:03:45.670
C-Could it be?

00:03:45.670 --> 00:03:46.640
A confession?

00:03:46.640 --> 00:03:47.450
Of love?

00:03:47.450 --> 00:03:48.440
How indecent.

00:03:48.440 --> 00:03:50.160
I'm not so sure.

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:56.080
Hey.

00:03:56.080 --> 00:03:56.920
What?

00:03:57.290 --> 00:03:59.090
Has she been getting closer lately?

00:03:59.090 --> 00:04:00.320
Don't ask me.

00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:01.340
I see.

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:03.340
What's different?

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:05.970
I got it! You finally started dating, right?

00:04:05.970 --> 00:04:07.940
Of course not.

00:04:08.260 --> 00:04:10.350
Then what's with her?

00:04:10.350 --> 00:04:12.270
That's what I'd like to know!

00:04:12.510 --> 00:04:14.240
What on Earth is your deal?

00:04:15.140 --> 00:04:16.730
You're emotionally excited.

00:04:17.070 --> 00:04:20.990
How dare Tachibana take advantage 
of Ai Ai growing up overseas.

00:04:21.560 --> 00:04:26.120
I heard he's filling her head with nonsense
to make her a convenient girlfriend.

00:04:26.120 --> 00:04:27.370
Gross.

00:04:29.990 --> 00:04:32.120
Give me a break.

00:04:32.540 --> 00:04:35.560
Emotional instability is 
unsuitable for an ARKS.

00:04:38.580 --> 00:04:41.140
Hey, Itsuki. Come check this out.

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:43.530
Over here.

00:04:56.080 --> 00:04:57.150
That was a three-pointer.

00:04:57.150 --> 00:04:58.380
Wow...

00:04:58.380 --> 00:05:01.440
Right? It's been like that the whole time.

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:03.920
But she shoots weird.

00:05:03.920 --> 00:05:05.200
Boys.

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:07.140
What are you doing?

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:08.450
Sorry.

00:05:09.530 --> 00:05:11.330
Well, that should do it.

00:05:11.980 --> 00:05:13.320
I have a question.

00:05:13.320 --> 00:05:15.660
What is it, Suzuki-san?

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:17.560
According to this material,

00:05:17.560 --> 00:05:19.820
the western army had captured 
strategic locations

00:05:19.820 --> 00:05:23.380
and surrounded their enemies 
on one side with a v-formation,

00:05:23.380 --> 00:05:24.840
so why did they lose?

00:05:25.580 --> 00:05:26.990
Well, well.

00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:29.350
The western army's greatest downfall

00:05:29.350 --> 00:05:34.680
was likely the betrayal of the 
Kobayakawa Clan stationed at Mt. Matsuo.

00:05:34.680 --> 00:05:37.020
I see. A betrayal.

00:05:37.260 --> 00:05:40.920
But why doesn't the Kobayakawa Clan 
appear later during the Edo Period

00:05:40.920 --> 00:05:44.070
if they played such a critical role?

00:05:44.960 --> 00:05:46.820
That's a very good question.

00:05:46.820 --> 00:05:52.720
It's said that Tokugawa Ieyasu suddenly began
treating the clan coldly after Sekigahara.

00:05:52.720 --> 00:05:54.540
What is this?

00:05:52.720 --> 00:05:55.330
In the end, two years after 
the Battle of Sekigahara...

00:05:56.320 --> 00:06:00.240
At first, this meeting was only
supposed to involve secretarial officers,

00:06:00.940 --> 00:06:05.340
but they insisted that the student
council presidents take part as well.

00:06:05.640 --> 00:06:07.290
Isn't that today?

00:06:07.290 --> 00:06:08.070
Yes.

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:11.850
Isn't it about cooperating with our 
sister school for the school festival?

00:06:11.850 --> 00:06:13.160
Yes.

00:06:13.160 --> 00:06:15.970
The goal of this project 
is to keep costs down

00:06:15.970 --> 00:06:20.400
by sharing equipment with our sister school.

00:06:20.700 --> 00:06:23.770
In other words, we're reusing equipment.

00:06:24.210 --> 00:06:26.660
Don't be so blunt.

00:06:26.950 --> 00:06:28.280
We're trying to be tactful about it.

00:06:28.800 --> 00:06:29.980
In any case,

00:06:30.620 --> 00:06:33.910
we'll need to carry an 
extensive list of equipment.

00:06:34.440 --> 00:06:35.910
You'll be attending the meeting, too.

00:06:36.340 --> 00:06:38.300
Vice President, we're counting on you.

00:06:38.560 --> 00:06:41.540
In other words, you want me to carry stuff.

00:06:41.900 --> 00:06:44.040
Well, yes.

00:06:44.400 --> 00:06:47.160
No tact there, huh?

00:06:49.440 --> 00:06:50.750
All right!

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:53.390
I'm on fire today.

00:06:53.390 --> 00:06:54.810
That was amazing.

00:06:56.420 --> 00:07:00.960
Um, what's your relationship with Suzuki-san?

00:07:01.250 --> 00:07:02.780
Where did that come from?

00:07:02.780 --> 00:07:03.940
Well...

00:07:06.960 --> 00:07:09.250
What is Suzuki-san doing here?

00:07:09.820 --> 00:07:11.570
I don't know, myself.

00:07:12.210 --> 00:07:14.200
Are the rumors true? Are you dating?

00:07:15.360 --> 00:07:17.330
I just happened to get on

00:07:17.920 --> 00:07:20.080
and just happened to sit in front of you.

00:07:20.770 --> 00:07:24.190
Is it true that you're forcing her to wait on you
and lie about it when people ask?

00:07:26.090 --> 00:07:27.250
By the way,

00:07:27.250 --> 00:07:31.840
the bus has been stopping at and 
passing the various stopping points.

00:07:32.220 --> 00:07:34.600
What kind of route does this vessel follow?

00:07:34.830 --> 00:07:39.350
Oh, it doesn't stop if 
nobody's getting on or off.

00:07:39.660 --> 00:07:42.480
Ah, so you express your desire to disembark.

00:07:43.940 --> 00:07:45.540
<i>Stop requested.</i>

00:07:45.900 --> 00:07:46.730
You're getting off?

00:07:47.280 --> 00:07:48.690
What's this button?

00:07:49.230 --> 00:07:52.040
Sorry, we made a mistake.

00:07:52.040 --> 00:07:53.480
We're not getting off.

00:07:54.440 --> 00:07:57.490
Next time, ask <i>before</i> you push any buttons.

00:07:57.840 --> 00:07:58.810
I see.

00:07:59.170 --> 00:08:01.300
So you use this button to express 
your intent to disembark.

00:08:01.590 --> 00:08:04.500
I'm impressed, Itsuki. 
That was a very clear explanation.

00:08:04.840 --> 00:08:06.690
You really are dating, aren't you?

00:08:06.690 --> 00:08:09.000
I told you, we're not.

00:08:10.790 --> 00:08:12.260
You don't believe me.

00:08:12.900 --> 00:08:17.080
If your friends don't trust you, 
you're not qualified to be an ARKS.

00:08:17.330 --> 00:08:18.880
Listen, you...

00:08:19.870 --> 00:08:24.600
By the way, Suzuki-san, 
you seem to know a lot about <i>PSO2</i>.

00:08:25.160 --> 00:08:29.110
Do you study ARKS like you study history?

00:08:29.560 --> 00:08:32.160
You want to know about ARKS activities?

00:08:33.090 --> 00:08:35.240
ARKS engage in a variety of activities.

00:08:35.720 --> 00:08:38.920
They primarily investigate the 
Darkers' degree of encroachment

00:08:39.180 --> 00:08:40.860
by visiting various planets,

00:08:40.860 --> 00:08:43.380
searching for Darkers and 
objects invaded by Darkers...

00:08:45.170 --> 00:08:47.910
Due to this, we must be careful at this time.

00:08:47.910 --> 00:08:50.750
Uh, sorry. I couldn't get all that.

00:08:53.220 --> 00:08:56.690
Suzuki-san, let's play 
<i>PSO2</i> together sometime.

00:08:56.690 --> 00:08:59.510
I'll send you a friend request. 
What's your character's name?

00:08:59.510 --> 00:09:02.520
My character? My name is Aika.

00:09:04.230 --> 00:09:06.360
You use your real name, too?

00:09:06.600 --> 00:09:10.740
Using your own name makes you feel more 
empathy for your character, doesn't it?

00:09:10.980 --> 00:09:13.140
<i>Th-They both use their real names...</i>

00:09:13.390 --> 00:09:17.120
Ending the battle against them
is the ARKS' goal.

00:09:17.450 --> 00:09:18.910
Don't you agree?

00:09:18.910 --> 00:09:21.410
Is this some kind of roleplay?

00:09:21.410 --> 00:09:23.160
Roleplay?

00:09:23.160 --> 00:09:24.760
N-Never mind.

00:09:25.030 --> 00:09:27.140
Of course we share the same goal.

00:09:27.410 --> 00:09:32.170
Then I suppose we should thank the 
Darkers for bringing us together.

00:09:32.690 --> 00:09:34.550
Thank the Darkers?

00:09:34.550 --> 00:09:35.800
What are you talking about?

00:09:36.420 --> 00:09:40.930
Do you have any idea how many 
ARKS they've hurt or killed?

00:09:40.930 --> 00:09:42.840
Actually, uh...

00:09:45.760 --> 00:09:49.190
I'm sorry. I became too emotional.

00:09:49.470 --> 00:09:51.140
I-It's fine.

00:09:51.140 --> 00:09:53.690
I shouldn't have been so thoughtless.

00:09:54.260 --> 00:09:56.570
Now arriving at Tensei Academy High School.

00:10:00.600 --> 00:10:03.180
Suzuki-san, you have business here, too?

00:10:03.180 --> 00:10:05.700
Yes, I came here for a reason.

00:10:05.960 --> 00:10:06.740
Farewell.

00:10:11.080 --> 00:10:13.780
What business could Suzuki-san have?

00:10:13.780 --> 00:10:14.820
Beats me.

00:10:14.820 --> 00:10:16.030
Excuse me.

00:10:17.340 --> 00:10:20.720
You're with the Seiga Academy 
student council, right?

00:10:21.160 --> 00:10:22.100
Yes.

00:10:22.100 --> 00:10:25.220
Thanks for coming. The student council 
president is waiting for you.

00:10:25.540 --> 00:10:28.800
I'm student council president Izumi Rina.

00:10:29.100 --> 00:10:30.900
This is my vice president...

00:10:30.900 --> 00:10:32.480
Tachibana Itsuki.

00:10:32.820 --> 00:10:36.230
We'll show you to the student council office.

00:10:43.780 --> 00:10:48.620
<b>[NPC]</b> Short for non-player character, characters appearing in the game world controlled by the game's system. The more powerful the program, the more human-like they appear. There are countless NPCs in PSO2 as well, serving as ARKS, shopkeepers, idols, and in various other capacities.

00:10:48.620 --> 00:10:53.420
<b>[Friend]</b> Connections formed online. Friendships are formed through a businesslike process unlikely to ever occur in the real world, in which one player submits a friend request and the receiving party accepts it. In PSO2, friends are able to send mail directly to each other and see if their friends are logged in.

00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:55.110
Thank you.

00:10:56.050 --> 00:10:57.470
Thank <i>you</i>.

00:10:57.590 --> 00:11:00.680
<b>Tensei Academy High School's List of Equipment to Borrow</b>

00:10:58.550 --> 00:11:01.890
We've got a lot of equipment to take with us.

00:11:02.280 --> 00:11:06.120
It might be faster to have it shipped.

00:11:06.400 --> 00:11:07.430
You're right.

00:11:08.120 --> 00:11:10.190
By the way, Suzuki-san...

00:11:10.500 --> 00:11:11.500
I wonder...

00:11:11.500 --> 00:11:14.080
Do you suppose she knows 
someone at this school?

00:11:14.410 --> 00:11:17.860
There's also a huge shopping mall nearby.

00:11:17.860 --> 00:11:19.260
Maybe she went there.

00:11:19.510 --> 00:11:21.200
Let's go there, then.

00:11:21.200 --> 00:11:22.300
What? Why?

00:11:22.570 --> 00:11:24.850
I'm interested in her.

00:11:25.120 --> 00:11:27.270
I guess I can't just ignore her.

00:11:27.270 --> 00:11:29.780
Senpai, it's this way, not that way.

00:11:40.210 --> 00:11:42.800
We don't know if she actually came here.

00:11:43.100 --> 00:11:45.990
Suzuki-san is a little strange, isn't she?

00:11:45.990 --> 00:11:48.810
She's been acting particularly 
strange the past few days.

00:11:49.400 --> 00:11:53.920
But she's been pretty weird 
since she transferred here.

00:11:53.920 --> 00:11:54.810
Really?

00:11:55.250 --> 00:11:59.070
It could be because she 
just returned from abroad.

00:11:59.430 --> 00:12:02.720
I see. She was raised overseas.

00:12:04.770 --> 00:12:05.570
Is that...

00:12:05.830 --> 00:12:06.760
There she is.

00:12:09.320 --> 00:12:10.460
What's wrong?

00:12:10.460 --> 00:12:11.340
Nothing.

00:12:12.700 --> 00:12:13.800
Her shoulder...

00:12:13.800 --> 00:12:15.210
What are you talking about?

00:12:15.740 --> 00:12:18.120
Is she smiling?

00:12:26.120 --> 00:12:28.250
Senpai, are you okay?

00:12:28.250 --> 00:12:28.970
Suzuki-san.

00:12:30.640 --> 00:12:32.440
Ah, Student Council President.

00:12:32.440 --> 00:12:33.400
What about your business?

00:12:33.400 --> 00:12:34.640
It's been concluded.

00:12:34.640 --> 00:12:38.980
I come here occasionally, since it's 
reminiscent of the ARKS shopping area.

00:12:39.350 --> 00:12:41.870
Now that you mention it, 
it is kind of similar.

00:12:42.220 --> 00:12:43.980
You like pet shops?

00:12:44.270 --> 00:12:45.050
Yes.

00:12:45.370 --> 00:12:46.990
Watching living creatures

00:12:48.720 --> 00:12:49.950
helps me relax.

00:12:51.820 --> 00:12:53.560
Are you sure you're okay?

00:12:53.560 --> 00:12:54.250
I'm fine.

00:12:55.270 --> 00:12:59.500
<i>Leaving her parents to live alone
in a strange place,</i>

00:12:59.500 --> 00:13:03.310
<i>she comes to see animals to seek out
the tiniest bit of warmth.</i>

00:13:03.880 --> 00:13:06.760
<i>I'm sorry I didn't understand until now.</i>

00:13:08.780 --> 00:13:09.760
What is it?

00:13:10.050 --> 00:13:11.530
<i>I can see clearly now.</i>

00:13:11.840 --> 00:13:13.770
<i>This feeling must be my maternal instinct.</i>

00:13:14.170 --> 00:13:17.270
Itsuki, what's wrong with the president?

00:13:17.270 --> 00:13:19.020
I-I'm not sure.

00:13:19.510 --> 00:13:21.560
Don't worry.

00:13:21.560 --> 00:13:24.030
If ever need any help, you can ask me.

00:13:24.030 --> 00:13:25.920
Help?

00:13:27.240 --> 00:13:29.240
Well, I don't have many clothes.

00:13:29.540 --> 00:13:31.540
Then I'll help you pick some out.

00:13:49.180 --> 00:13:52.680
<b>Itsuki</b>

00:13:49.180 --> 00:13:52.680
<b>Student Council!</b>

00:13:49.180 --> 00:13:52.680
<b>Rina</b>

00:13:49.180 --> 00:13:52.680
<b>Aika</b>

00:13:49.180 --> 00:13:52.680
<b>First Photo</b>

00:13:53.130 --> 00:13:56.430
Thanks to you, I was able to acquire 
some local clothing. I'm grateful.

00:13:56.760 --> 00:13:58.160
I'm glad.

00:13:59.450 --> 00:14:00.490
What is it?

00:14:00.780 --> 00:14:02.940
There's a kid crying.

00:14:04.100 --> 00:14:06.060
What happened?

00:14:06.370 --> 00:14:07.640
My balloon...

00:14:08.080 --> 00:14:09.330
Did it fly away?

00:14:12.100 --> 00:14:12.950
Is that it?

00:14:14.940 --> 00:14:16.960
It's a bit too high up.

00:14:17.680 --> 00:14:19.280
I can reach it by jumping.

00:14:19.280 --> 00:14:19.960
What?

00:14:27.780 --> 00:14:29.720
A-Amazing...

00:14:31.070 --> 00:14:31.850
Here.

00:14:32.530 --> 00:14:34.100
Don't let go anymore.

00:14:34.470 --> 00:14:36.100
Okay, thanks.

00:14:36.580 --> 00:14:38.790
Where are your daddy and mommy?

00:14:39.030 --> 00:14:39.890
What?

00:14:41.780 --> 00:14:44.280
Mommy? Mommy?

00:14:46.120 --> 00:14:47.170
Mommy?

00:14:50.190 --> 00:14:52.140
So she's lost.

00:14:52.600 --> 00:14:54.120
She's missing?

00:14:54.620 --> 00:14:55.800
What's your name?

00:14:56.590 --> 00:14:57.690
Asuka.

00:14:57.690 --> 00:15:02.520
Asuka-chan, it looks like your mommy 
is playing hide and seek with you.

00:15:03.070 --> 00:15:04.330
Hide and seek?

00:15:04.330 --> 00:15:05.040
Yeah.

00:15:05.400 --> 00:15:08.840
Now, where do you think 
your mommy is hiding?

00:15:08.840 --> 00:15:10.550
Uh, um...

00:15:10.550 --> 00:15:11.450
That way.

00:15:21.420 --> 00:15:22.900
Mommy, where are you?

00:15:23.500 --> 00:15:24.400
Asuka!

00:15:26.460 --> 00:15:27.150
Mommy!

00:15:27.590 --> 00:15:28.910
I found you.

00:15:28.910 --> 00:15:30.110
Asuka.

00:15:30.900 --> 00:15:32.630
You shouldn't have done that.

00:15:30.900 --> 00:15:33.150
Thank goodness. What a relief.

00:15:35.410 --> 00:15:38.180
Let's play together again.

00:15:39.340 --> 00:15:40.410
You can have these.

00:15:41.530 --> 00:15:42.360
Here.

00:15:44.440 --> 00:15:45.380
Thank you.

00:15:45.380 --> 00:15:46.440
Bye-bye.

00:15:54.560 --> 00:15:56.550
I acquired some items.

00:16:01.200 --> 00:16:03.560
It tastes like a Photon Drink.

00:16:04.060 --> 00:16:08.570
Senpai, that was sharp of you to say 
her mom was playing hide and seek.

00:16:08.870 --> 00:16:12.420
I personally don't enjoy 
hide and seek, though.

00:16:12.420 --> 00:16:13.180
